---
import Shell from '../layouts/Shell.astro';
---
<Shell
  current="home"
  title="The Grid — hazard, road & weather data for the central Sierra"
  description="Public, keyless, real-time hazard, road, and weather data for the central Sierra — wildfire, evacuation, weather, earthquake, road incidents and power outages unified into one honest API. Run by S.I.E.R.R.A, a volunteer emergency-response alliance."
>
  <style is:global slot="head">
    /* Page-local: the deck's static skeleton and the front-page feed. Every
       color/size resolves to an app.css token — the deck, ledger, record row
       and numbered section head are all shared primitives (app.css §14). */

    /* TOP OF THE FEED — the lead record, set larger than the rows beneath it. */
    /* The lead record carries the same 6px severity spine as the rows beneath
       it — it is usually the most severe item on the page and was the only one
       rendered unmarked. */
    /* The SAME hairline as the rows beneath it. A 3px black rule here read as a
       section divider and broke the feed into "one thing, then a list" — but the
       lead is the first item OF that list. Its prominence comes from the display
       size and its severity spine, not from a heavier separator. */
    .lead-rec {
      border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule); padding-bottom: 12px; margin-bottom: 0;
      padding-left: 18px; box-shadow: inset 6px 0 0 var(--text-tertiary);
    }
    .lead-rec.sev-EXTREME { box-shadow: inset 6px 0 0 var(--sev-EXTREME); }
    .lead-rec.sev-SEVERE { box-shadow: inset 6px 0 0 var(--sev-SEVERE); }
    .lead-rec.sev-MODERATE { box-shadow: inset 6px 0 0 var(--sev-MODERATE); }
    .lead-rec.sev-MINOR { box-shadow: inset 6px 0 0 var(--sev-MINOR); }
    .lead-rec.sev-INFO { box-shadow: inset 6px 0 0 var(--sev-INFO); }
    .lead-rec .lead-head {
      font-family: var(--font-display); font-weight: 900;
      font-size: clamp(24px, 3vw, 34px); line-height: 1.06; letter-spacing: -0.03em;
      color: var(--text-primary); margin: 6px 0 8px; text-wrap: balance;
    }
    .lead-rec a { text-decoration: none; }
    .lead-rec a:hover .lead-head { color: var(--signal); }
    .lead-meta { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 10px; color: var(--text-muted-p); letter-spacing: 0.04em; }
    .feed-rows { margin-bottom: 8px; }

    /* 02 — three contract columns. .cap-grid/.cap-card are the shared columns. */
    .contracts { margin-top: 10px; }
    .cap-eyebrow {
      font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 9.5px; letter-spacing: 0.14em;
      text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--text-tertiary); margin-bottom: 6px;
    }

    .sec { margin-top: var(--space-section); }
    .sec-body { max-width: var(--measure); font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.55; color: var(--text-2nd); }
  </style>

  <!-- ================= THE DECK (black, full-bleed) ================= -->
  <!-- Rendered empty and filled by JS: every figure in it is a live value, and
       a fabricated placeholder number here would be exactly the "absence read as
       an all-clear" the contract forbids. The pending state says so in words. -->
  <div class="deck" id="deck" slot="deck">
    <div class="deck-inner">
      <div class="dateline" id="deck-dateline">
        <span>fetching place summary…</span>
      </div>
      <h1 class="hero" id="deck-hero">Loading the current state of the region…</h1>
      <div class="subline" id="deck-subline"></div>
      <div class="deck-body">
      <p class="deck-lede">
        The Grid is the public data service of S.I.E.R.R.A — a volunteer 501(c)(3)
        serving the central Sierra. Wildfire, evacuation, weather, earthquake,
        road incidents and power outages from a dozen upstream feeds, normalized into one queryable
        event model with full revision history. Read-only, keyless, CORS-open.
      </p>
      <div class="ledger" id="deck-ledger">
        <div class="ledger-cell"><div class="ledger-v">—</div><div class="ledger-l">Events · extreme</div></div>
        <div class="ledger-cell"><div class="ledger-v">—</div><div class="ledger-l">Events · severe</div></div>
        <div class="ledger-cell"><div class="ledger-v">—</div><div class="ledger-l">Events · moderate</div></div>
        <div class="ledger-cell ledger-cell-alt"><div class="ledger-v">—</div><div class="ledger-l">Evacuation zones</div></div>
      </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div id="deck-error"></div>

  <!-- ================= TOP OF THE FEED ================= -->
  <div class="sec" id="feed-sec">
    <div class="eyebrow">Top of the feed</div>
    <div id="feed-lead"><span class="loading">fetching /api/v1/events…</span></div>
    <div class="feed-rows" id="feed-rows"></div>
  </div>

  <!-- ================= 01 Your first request ================= -->
  <div class="sec">
    <div class="numbered-head"><span class="ord">01</span><h2>Your first request</h2></div>
    <p class="sec-body">
      There is no key, no signup and no CORS preflight to negotiate. The response
      below was fetched by this page, in your browser, from the same public
      endpoint your code would call — the button copies the exact curl.
    </p>
    <div class="resp-pane" id="first-req">
      <div class="resp-head">
        <span class="method">GET</span>
        <span id="first-req-path">/api/v1/events?place=…&amp;page_size=1</span>
        <button class="copy-btn" id="first-req-copy" type="button">copy curl</button>
      </div>
      <pre id="first-req-body">fetching…</pre>
      <div class="resp-foot" id="first-req-foot"></div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- ================= 02 Three contracts, not conventions ================= -->
  <div class="sec">
    <div class="numbered-head"><span class="ord">02</span><h2>Three contracts, not conventions</h2></div>
    <div class="cap-grid contracts">
      <div class="cap-card">
        <div class="cap-eyebrow">One model</div>
        <div class="cap-h">Every hazard, one query</div>
        <div class="cap-p">
          Wildfire, evacuation, weather alert, fire weather, earthquake, road
          incidents and power outages are normalized from a dozen upstream feeds into one event
          model with full revision history. Ask once; get the whole region.
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="cap-card marked">
        <div class="cap-eyebrow">Fail loud</div>
        <div class="cap-h">Absence is never an all-clear</div>
        <div class="cap-p">
          Every feed reports <span class="mono">OK</span> / <span class="mono">STALE</span> /
          <span class="mono">UNAVAILABLE</span>, and a failure is rendered as a failure —
          <span class="mono">null</span> means <em>unknown</em>, never zero. Life-safety
          data you can trust <em>because</em> it tells you when it can't.
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="cap-card">
        <div class="cap-eyebrow">Unprivileged</div>
        <div class="cap-h">Built to be built on</div>
        <div class="cap-p">
          Public, keyless, CORS-open, RFC 7946 GeoJSON. Any website, map client or
          radio-room dashboard can consume it directly. This site is just one
          client of the same API — nothing here is privileged.
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- ================= 03 Conventions ================= -->
  <div class="sec">
    <div class="numbered-head"><span class="ord">03</span><h2>Conventions</h2></div>
    <dl class="def-rows" id="conventions"></dl>
  </div>

  <!-- ================= Support ================= -->
  <div class="support-card">
    <h2>Keep this service running</h2>
    <p class="support-p">
      S.I.E.R.R.A is an all-volunteer 501(c)(3). This service runs on donated time and a small
      cloud bill — the feeds, the servers, and the radio infrastructure behind them. The page
      you're on is the case for support: it's live, it's honest about what it doesn't know, and
      anyone can verify or build on it. If an open, always-on data source for the central Sierra
      is worth keeping online, please help fund it.
    </p>
    <a class="btn-primary" href="https://sierragridteam.org/donate" rel="noopener">Donate</a>
    <a class="btn-ghost" href="/docs">Read the API reference</a>
  </div>

  <script is:inline type="module" src="/assets/pages/home.js"></script>
</Shell>
